<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alyattes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 610–560 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as Alyattes of Lydia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alyattes was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydia">Lydia</a> from around 610 to 560 BCE, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mermnad-dynasty">Mermnad dynasty</a>, and father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croesus">Croesus</a>. He expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimmerians">Cimmerians</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, destroyed Smyrna, and fought a long war with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/median-empire">Median Empire</a> that ended after the solar eclipse of 585 BCE with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kizilirmak">Halys</a> river as the border. His huge burial mound at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bin-tepe">Bin Tepe</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardis">Sardis</a> survives.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alyattes.jpg" alt="Alyattes" width="320" height="133" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KINGS_of_LYDIA._Alyattes._Circa_620-10-564-53_BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
